.TH COMMAND * 2014-04-08 "SequoiaDB" "Sequoiadb Method's Manual"
.ad l.ll 72.ce 1000
\fBtraceFmt()\fR
.ce 0
.sp 2

.SH "NAME"

.sp 2
traceFmt

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp 2

.sp 2

.sp 2
traceFmt( \fB<formatType>, <input>,<input>\fR )
.SH "CATEGORY"

.sp 2

.sp 2
Golbal
.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.sp 2
The trace file exported by db.traceOff() is in binary format and is not
convenient for users to read.
This command can be used to format the trace file into user\-readable content
and output it to the specified file.
.sp 2
.SH "PARAMETERS"
.sp 2
\fBformatType ( int )\fR

\fBformatType can take the following two values:\fR	   
.br	   
	  0: The database engine tracking program will record the tracking information in the output file according to the process number.
.br	   
	  1: The database engine tracking program will record the tracking information in the output file according to the temporal order.   
.sp 2
\fBinput ( string )\fR
.br
       Input file.
.sp 2
\fBoutput ( String )\fR
.br
       Output file.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.sp 2
On success, return void.
.sp 2
On error, exception will be thrown.
.sp 2
.SH "ERRORS"
.sp 2
when exception happen, use getLastError() to get the error code and use
getLastErrMsg() to get error message.
For more detial, please reference to Troubleshooting.

.SH "Examples"

.sp 2
Formatted the output file
.sp 2
>\ traceFmt( 0, "/opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump", "/opt/sequoiadb/trace.output" )

Using traceStatus() to view the tracking status of the current program.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceStatus()
.sp 2